(2759546, 384132, 62671, '<td valign="top">a blue sky with poofy white clouds would have made this phenomenal.  Did you shoot with a polorizer?  If not, you need one.  I love the fence line.  the one in the foreground draws your eye back to the one that cuts across at the trees.  With an overexposed white sky I would have cropped more of it off.  If this was advanced editing I would have replaced it in photoshop.  <br/>I think a grad ND filter would have been helpful here too but I don''t have one yet to give advice on using it.  I love this image anyway so Im adding it to my favorites!</td>', 'a blue sky with poofy white clouds would have made this phenomenal.  Did you shoot with a polorizer?  If not, you need one.  I love the fence line.  the one in the foreground draws your eye back to the one that cuts across at the trees.  With an overexposed white sky I would have cropped more of it off.  If this was advanced editing I would have replaced it in photoshop.  I think a grad ND filter would have been helpful here too but I don''t have one yet to give advice on using it.  I love this image anyway so Im adding it to my favorites!', '2006-08-25 12:14:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2759549, 383629, 16004, '<td valign="top">gorgeous.  another (typically) brilliant example on the joys of IR when you have someone who knows what they''re doing behind the lens!  however, the decision to keep the pink on the trees is genius; gives it a great effect and does differentiate from what you would expect.  it''s really beautiful, and the mirror like flat water only enhances that.  only minor criticism is that for the challenge focus doesn''t feel soft enough.  it has that glow, certainly, but i don''t know, it just doesn''t say it''s any softer than any IR photo.  so, err, 9!</td>', 'gorgeous.  another (typically) brilliant example on the joys of IR when you have someone who knows what they''re doing behind the lens!  however, the decision to keep the pink on the trees is genius; gives it a great effect and does differentiate from what you would expect.  it''s really beautiful, and the mirror like flat water only enhances that.  only minor criticism is that for the challenge focus doesn''t feel soft enough.  it has that glow, certainly, but i don''t know, it just doesn''t say it''s any softer than any IR photo.  so, err, 9!', '2006-08-25 12:16:15.000000', NULL, 1),
